  "criteria": "1) Use Service Quotas (service code 'bedrock') to list applied vs default values for key quotas: on-demand InvokeModel/Converse requests per minute and tokens per minute for the models actually in use or enabled (e.g. Anthropic Claude, Amazon Nova/Titan), provisioned throughput model units, concurrent batch jobs, knowledge base/agent/guardrail limits, and cross-region inference quotas. 2) Identify which models are actually used (CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics: Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, InvocationThrottles, InvocationClientErrors/ServerErrors, InvocationLatency) and compute peak per-minute usage vs applied quota (percent utilization). Flag any throttles. 3) Check whether models are enabled/accessible (list foundation models/inference profiles if possible). 4) Note quota increase requests pending/history. Report a concise table of quota, applied value, peak observed usage, headroom %, and a verdict (OK / watch / at risk). If there is no Bedrock usage yet, say so and report the applied quotas relative to default so the user can judge expected production load. State clearly any data you could not access."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock quota limits and usage headroom"}, {"id": "tooluse_0Y5vPmgqg57CG5bDlMd07G", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-retention-posture", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["aiml-bedrock-security-assessment", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
