  "context": "User asks 'Are we ready to run Bedrock in production?' and specifically wants the data-retention posture. This slice covers ONLY retention/logging/encryption/guardrail posture. Another sub-agent covers quota headroom, so do not duplicate that. Follow the aiml-bedrock-security-assessment skill if available.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1 (also check other associated AWS accounts via list_associations if any)", "Region us-east-1 as primary; also check other regions where Bedrock resources exist"],
  "timeframe": "Current state",
  "criteria": "Check: 1) Model invocation logging configuration (enabled? destinations CloudWatch Logs/S3, whether prompts/responses/embeddings are logged). 2) Retention of those destinations: CloudWatch log group retention days, S3 bucket lifecycle rules, versioning, encryption (KMS), public access block, Object Lock. 3) KMS encryption of Bedrock resources (custom models, knowledge bases, agents, guardrails, batch job output, model customization data). 4) Guardrails coverage (PII filters, content filters) and whether agents/knowledge bases use them. 5) VPC endpoints for bedrock/bedrock-runtime and PrivateLink policies. 6) CloudTrail coverage for Bedrock API calls and CloudWatch alarms. 7) Knowledge base vector store data retention/encryption and agent session/memory retention settings. 8) Any IAM least-privilege issues for roles with bedrock:* access (report only). Provide severity-rated findings (Critical/High/Medium/Low) with a short remediation for each, and an overall verdict on retention posture. If Bedrock is not in use at all, say so explicitly and report which baseline controls are not yet in place. State clearly any data you could not access."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review Bedrock data retention and security posture"}], "created_at": null}

